## Context

The beat raid currently closes tickets by editing `.erg` files directly with
the `Edit` tool. This is blocked by Claude Code permission checks on
sensitive-file edits, and when it succeeds it can still leave tickets in
`doing` state if the agent exits before committing (the double-pick bug,
ticket 0037 in the harness).

An `erg close` command makes closure atomic: one shell call, no Edit tool,
no permission issue. The beat can call it and then `git commit`.

## Actions

1. Add `cmdClose(args []string) int` to `main.go`:
   - Usage: `erg close <id-or-file> <reason>`
   - Accept 4-digit ID or file path
   - Find file: for ID, glob `tickets/{id}-*.erg`; for path, use directly
   - Read Status header; if already `closed`, print `ALREADY_CLOSED` and exit 0
   - Replace `Status: <anything>` → `Status: closed`
   - Append log line: `{ISO8601} claude status closed — {reason}`
   - Remove `.git/ticket-wip/{id}.wip` if present (idempotent)
   - Print `CLOSED` on success
   - Exit non-zero on: file not found, ambiguous ID, parse error

2. Wire into `main()` dispatch: `case "close": exitCode = cmdClose(rest)`

3. Update `printUsage()` with the new command.

4. Add tests in `main_test.go`:
   - Close an open ticket → Status becomes closed, log appended
   - Close already-closed ticket → ALREADY_CLOSED, exit 0 (idempotent)
   - Close by file path → works
   - Missing ID → non-zero exit

## Out of scope

- `erg claim`, `erg release` — separate ticket (0006 remainder)
- Modularization of main.go — separate ticket (0006 remainder)
- IDH skill updates — separate harness ticket after binary ships

## Exit criteria

- `erg close 0006 "done"` closes the ticket atomically
- `erg close 0006 "done"` run twice: second call exits 0 with ALREADY_CLOSED
- All existing tests in `main_test.go` pass
- Binary rebuilt and copied to all project locations
